You need to read a large file and send it as an HTTP response. Which approach is best?

```js
// A
fs.readFile('large.csv', (err, data) => res.end(data));

// B
const stream = fs.createReadStream('large.csv');
stream.pipe(res);

// C
const data = fs.readFileSync('large.csv');
res.end(data);

// D
fetch('large.csv').then(r => r.text()).then(data => res.end(data));
```

What is the output of the following Node.js code?

```js
console.log('start');
setImmediate(() => console.log('immediate'));
process.nextTick(() => console.log('nextTick'));
console.log('end');
```

You build an Express middleware that logs request duration. Where should you call `next()` and where should you record the end time?

```js
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const start = Date.now();
  // WHERE does the timing logic go?
  next();
});
```

An Express route handler throws an error inside an async function, but Express's default error handler never receives it. What is the fix?

```js
app.get('/user/:id', async (req, res) => {
  const user = await db.findUser(req.params.id); // can throw
  res.json(user);
});
```

A developer writes an HTTP server where each request creates an interval:

```js
app.get('/stream', (req, res) => {
  const id = setInterval(() => res.write('ping'), 1000);
  res.on('close', () => clearInterval(id));
});
```

